+## Run and analysis modes
+
+`build()` defaults to `mode="run"`. This retains executable relationships, selected
+registration discovery, ordinary scopes, providers, ownership, cleanup and warmup
+plans. It releases graph inspection evidence and composition for future overlays.
+
+Use `build(mode="analysis")` for graph traversal, explanations, manifests, census,
+architecture reports and full validation. Analysis captures diagnostics, checks
+reachability and validates unused dependency-only declarations. It retains the
+blueprint needed by `new_scope_builder()`. Neither mode activates application
+constructors during compilation.
+
+| Capability | Run | Analysis |
+| --- | --- | --- |
+| Resolution, filters, providers/maps, ordinary scopes and cleanup | Supported | Supported |
+| `components`, `selected_registrations`, warmups, profiling | Supported | Supported |
+| Mandatory structural checks and build-mode rules | Always | Always |
+| Graph inspection, explanations, census and manifests | Unavailable | Complete supported evidence |
+| Unreachable advisories and unused dependency-only validation | Omitted | Included |
+| `validation_report()` | Unavailable | Explicit full-validation pass |
+| New scope builders | Unavailable | Run or analysis children allowed |
+| Failure aggregation | Original failure; no independent root retries | Aggregate independent failures using existing retry safeguards |
+
+Run errors preserve mandatory findings and actionable captured code/path/triage
+information. Analysis errors additionally retain diagnostic history and partial
+graphs. A failed builder remains retryable. Analysis may invoke additional callbacks
+while validating unused declarations or aggregating failed roots; identical build
+callback counts are not promised across those extra operations.
+
+An analysis build runs build-mode rules once. Call `validation_report()` once to
+run validation-only rules and return their findings with stored build findings:
 
