+After successful run compilation, saved inspection graphs explicitly expire and
+release their context. Component snapshots outside the retained execution closure
+keep the established `explain-metadata-disabled` error; captured source-inspection
+snapshots remain caller-owned. Warmup and instrumentation descriptors are captured
+before reduction. Retaining builders, callbacks, snapshots or an analysis ancestor
+can retain application-owned data independently of the run runtime.
+
+### Overlay composition
+
+An analysis parent can produce either mode. A run child releases its blueprint
+and cannot create another scope builder. Ordinary child scopes inherit their
+parent's mode. Run parents reject `new_scope_builder()` and direct
+`ScopeBuilder(parent)` construction. Reducing a child does not mutate its parent's
+inspection graph or change inherited singleton ownership.
+
+### Analysis-only roots
+
+Analysis validates unused dependency-only declarations without exposing them to
+`resolve()`. Invalid unused declarations can therefore fail analysis while run
+succeeds. Graph roots expose `resolvable`; manifests mark nonpublic roots with
+`"resolvable": false`, and text rendering labels them `Inspect`. Promoting one
+of these declarations to a public root remains visible in semantic graph diffs.
+The selected executable catalogue is unaffected by these inspection-only roots.
 
